{"purpose":"Define v2 product requirements as software delivery standard: versioned lifecycle specification, framework-free runtime, distributed delivery lifecycle standards via registry.","content":"PRD-002 Anvil v2 — Software Delivery Standard. Supersedes PRD-001 and amendments per Transition Plan. Translates approved architecture (Manifesto → Transition Plan → ADR-021..036 → 006 overview) into product requirements without new architectural decisions. Defines delivery lifecycle standard: definition, enforcement, verification, state \u0026 observability, vocabulary, delivery lifecycle standards (framework content), distribution, compatibility, artifact lifecycle, release lifecycle, repository/version management, migration from v1.x, community contribution (gated). Users: solo dev, engineering team, framework maintainer, standard maintainer, organization, platform team, community contributor. Workflows: init, adopt/update standard, build/package, verify, deliver, install/activate, rollback, observe, migrate, author standard. Boundaries exclude CI scheduling, pipeline definition, mechanics, provisioning, monitoring, container orchestration, framework implementation, secrets, platform service. Architecture: Specification → Runtime → standards. Roadmap phases 0-7 per Transition Plan. Superseded PRD-001 sections marked historical. See docs/prd/PRD-002-anvil-v2.md."}